    "answer": {
      "short": "$71$",
      "worked": "Match $1$, $-x^{-1}$ and $x^{-2}$ with the constant, linear and quadratic terms of $(1+2x)^7$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Constant term}&=1-\\binom{7}{1}2+\\binom{7}{2}2^2\\\\\\text{Constant term}&=1-14+84\\\\\\text{Constant term}&=71.\\end{align*}$$",
